# Kettle Linux: keep the Adreno 740 powered between frames (runtime PM "on"). When it powers
# down, the GMU sometimes fails to power it back up ("Timeout waiting for GMU OOB set GPU_SET"),
# the GPU then runs with its state lost (a CP fault at address 0) and the driver's recovery can
# hang the display for good. With the GPU kept powered there were none in hours of use, games
# included; the cost is some battery while idle. A workaround until the kernel's GMU wake-up is
# fixed; system sleep still powers it off.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", KERNEL=="3d00000.gpu", ATTR{power/control}="on"
